1375,5189],[890,5189],[1558,5188],[1690,5187],[1205,5187],[1694,5186],[1209,5186],[1832,5185],[1347,5185],[1830,5184],[1345,5184],[1462,5183],[977,5183],[1081,5182],[1590,5181],[1415,5180],[930,5180],[1707,5179],[1222,5179],[1094,5178],[1386,5177],[901,5177],[1364,5176],[1411,5175],[926,5175],[1777,5174],[1292,5174],[1103,5173],[1704,5172],[1219,5172],[1416,5171],[931,5171],[1706,5170],[1221,5170],[1712,5169],[1227,5169],[1724,5168],[1239,5168],[1486,5167],[1001,5167],[1380,5166],[895,5166],[1482,5165],[997,5165],[1412,5164],[927,5164],[1459,5163],[974,5163],[1660,5162],[1175,5162],[1786,5161],[1301,5161],[1433,5160],[948,5160],[1435,5159],[950,5159],[1471,5158],[986,5158],[1359,5157],[1478,5156],[993,5156],[1392,5155],[907,5155],[1516,5154],[1031,5154],[1730,5153],[1245,5153],[1472,5152],[987,5152],[1448,5151],[963,5151],[1775,5150],[1290,5150],[1372,5149],[887,5149],[1618,5148],[1133,5148],[1485,5147],[1000,5147],[1374,5146],[889,5146],[1687,5145],[1202,5145],[1559,5144],"Your first minutes","your defaults: `~/.config/brokspace` (Linux),\n`~/Library/Application Support/brokspace` (macOS), `%APPDATA%\\brokspace`\n(Windows);","Writing your own","writes the choice to `.brokspace/brok.yml` (`llm.default`).","Write your own:","Workspace skills in `.brokspace/skills/<name>/` **override** built-ins with\nthe same name, so you can tailor any built-in to your team. Keep skills\nshort and explicit: small local models follow them too. The built-in\n`write-skill` skill walks your agent through it.","Workspace layout","working directory = workspace root;","Without a GPU the model runs on the processor: memory decides what fits,\nbut speed decides what is pleasant. A laptop CPU reads a long prompt into a\n7B model at about 15 tokens per second, so a review takes 3 to 5 minutes;\na 3B model is about twice as fast. That is why machines without a GPU get\none size smaller. Only NVIDIA GPUs and Apple Silicon are detected; with\nanother GPU that Ollama supports, pick the row for your GPU memory.","Where the index is mirrored, configured with `brok setup sync`.","When something is specific to your team (a ticketing system, a deploy\npipeline, a compliance check), write a shard instead of waiting for a core\nfeature: it reacts to workspace events and publishes its own. See\nShards and start with `brok shard new my-integration`.","When names collide, the first wins: workspace (`.brokspace/skills/`) >\ninstalled shards > built-in. `brok skill list` reports shadowed skills.","What your machine can run","What you get","What to expect: 1B to 3B models answer questions about your code well\nenough (`brok ask`, `brok chat`), but they lose track of longer skills, so\n`brok review`, `brok commit` and most `brok skill run` workflows are much\nbetter with 7B or larger. Even at 7B, a review is a first pass that can be\nwrong; 14B and hosted models (`brok review -p anthropic`) review much\nbetter, and commit messages are already good at 7B.","What the runtime **enforces**: topic ACLs, `source` stamping, reply routing,\nthe scrubbed environment, the working directory.","What is **declared but not yet enforced by the OS**: file system and network\naccess. Consent at install time is the safeguard until OS sandboxes (Landlock,\nSeatbelt, AppContainer) land. `build.command` runs arbitrary code from the\nshard repository (e.g. `build.rs`) — the consent prompt shows it before it\nruns. Prefer shards that publish checksum-pinned `releases`.","Well-known topics","Want no questions? `brok init --yes` accepts every recommendation.\nThen check the result:","validates `shard.json` and the `brok` version requirement;","Using the SDK","Using the same model elsewhere","Using skills","uses a model you already have, or offers to download the recommended one\n(`ollama pull`);","User defaults","Use it every day","Update brok","Unknown fields are rejected, and all violations are reported at once.","Uninstall","Uma IDE com o Brokspace embutido, para o modo IDE ao lado da CLI brok.","Types live in `brok_sdk::payload`.","Typed payloads implement `brok_sdk::Payload` (a serde type plus its topic).","Two ways to use it","Two kinds","Tudo também está no menu **Brokspace** e na paleta de comandos: Configurar\nWorkspace, Iniciar / Parar / Reiniciar, Reconstruir Índice, Diagnóstico,\nInstalar, Criar e Remover Shard, Exportar Skills para Agentes de Código,\nExecutar Skill, Revisar, Escrever Mensagem de Commit. A barra de status\nmostra se o Brokspace está rodando e qual modelo ele usa.","Troubleshooting","Topics","Today, build your own with Shards and\nSkills, and start from the\nshard template.","Toda solicitação passa pelo `brok`, que a envia ao LLM definido em\n`.brokspace/brok.yml` (Ollama, LM Studio ou uma API hospedada compatível com\nOpenAI). Sem um LLM, ou quando ele não responde, o agente responde com o que\no índice local encontrou, em forma de links.","To trigger your shard by hand, publish the event it listens to:\n`brok bus emit file:changed '{\"changed\":[\"src/main.rs\"],\"deleted\":[]}'`.\nWindows PowerShell 5.1 drops the inner double quotes when it calls a\nprogram, so escape them there: `'{\\\"changed\\\":[\\\"src/main.rs\\\"],\\\"deleted\\\":[]}'`\n(PowerShell 7 and other shells need no escaping).","This document explains how the pieces of Brokspace fit together. It is aimed\nat contributors and shard authors.","This document explains how the pieces of Brokspace fit together.","Then run `brok skill export` in your workspaces so your coding agents get\nthe updated built-in skills.","Then delete:","The window starts minimal: Explorer, Search, Source Control and Brokspace on\nthe left, the **Brokspace agent** docked on the right. Debug, Testing and\nExtensions stay one shortcut away.","The skill's instructions (and the reference files it links) become the\nsystem prompt; Brokspace adds relevant code from the index as context.","The short version","the shared model cache: `~/.cache/brokspace` (Linux),\n`~/Library/Caches/brokspace` (macOS), `%LOCALAPPDATA%\\brokspace` (Windows);","The same workspace in an IDE built around it: a home page that starts\nwith your question, the Brokspace agent in the chat, search, reviews and\ncommit messages one click away.","The official home of shards, skills and agents for Brokspace.","the manifest's `build.command`, run in the repository;","The IDE updates itself from GitHub Releases. For answers you need an LLM:\nsee Local LLM setup (search works without one).","The IDE talks to Brokspace only through the `brok` CLI and its JSON output\n(see Integrations), so it shows exactly what `brok`\nsees, and anything it does you can also do in a terminal. It needs brok\n0.2.4 or newer; the one it ships with qualifies.","The IDE is in English and Brazilian Portuguese. It starts in Portuguese on a\nPortuguese system; switch with **Language** on the home page.","The Hub is being built. Until it opens, install shards from any git\nrepository with `brok shard install <url>`.","The first launch needs right click > **Open** while the app is not\nnotarized yet.","The first `ask`, `chat`, `review` or `commit` starts brok in the background.\nFrom then on the index follows you: saved files, commits, pulls and branch\nswitches are picked up within seconds.","The fastest way to write one is the\nbrok-shard-template\nrepository; this page is the reference.","The built-in workflows, and how to write and share your own.","The built-in workflows are adapted from\nmattpocock/skills (MIT); see\nskills/CREDITS.md.","The Brokspace view","The Brokspace Hub will be the official catalog of shards built by the\nBrokspace team, and later a registry anyone can publish to, in the spirit of\nDocker Hub:","The Brokspace agent","the `brok` and `brok-agent` programs (`~/.local/bin`, or\n`%LOCALAPPDATA%\\Programs\\brok` on Windows; `cargo uninstall brok-cli brok-agent`\nif you used Cargo).","the `.brokspace/` folder of each workspace (plus `.agents/skills`,\n`.claude/skills` and the MCP files if you no longer want them);","the **built-in skills**, such as `/ask-brok`, `/grill-me`, `/to-spec`,\n`tdd` and `code-review`.","Text-only search (embeddings disabled or model missing): BM25 postings in\nmemory plus memory-mapped chunk data; typically a few tens of MB.","Streaming events:","Stores","Stop (Ctrl+C, or `brok stop` publishing `daemon:stop`): broadcast\n`system:shutdown` → shards get 3 seconds to exit, then are killed → index\nservice stops → bus stops → runtime files removed.","Still stuck? Run `brok logs -n 100` and ask in\nDiscussions, including the\noutput of `brok doctor`.","stdout and stderr are captured line by line, prefixed with the shard name in\nthe `brok run` output and appended to `.brokspace/logs/<name>.log`. Log to\nstderr.","Start: bind the bus → issue the operator token (`run/operator.token`) → start\nthe control service (`daemon:status`, `daemon:stop`) → open the index for\nwriting (falls back to read-only search if the model or lock is unavailable),\ncatch up on changes made while stopped, and connect the index service → for\neach enabled shard, issue a token from its manifest, build its sandbox\nenvironment and supervise it.","Start with `brok doctor`: it checks everything and prints the fix.","Start","Small models (1.5b, 3b) are fine for questions (`ask`, `chat`); reviews and\ncommit messages are much better with 7b or larger. Without a GPU, a 7b\nmodel takes a few minutes per review, which is why the table suggests 3b\nthere.","Skills land in `.claude/skills/` and the portable `.agents/skills/` (read by\nCodex, Cursor, Copilot and others). Folders are marked `.brokspace-managed`\nand refreshed on every export; brok never overwrites a folder it did not\ncreate. Commit them to share with your team.","Skills","Sizes are for 4-bit quantized models (`Q4_K_M`), the best balance between\nspeed and quality.","Sharing skills: skill shards","Shards: integrations you build","Shards do not have to be written in Rust: anything that can open a Unix\nsocket / named pipe and exchange length-prefixed JSON frames works. The frame\nformat is documented in `brok-sdk/src/frame.rs` and `codec.rs`.","Shards are small programs that react to workspace events. Each one is a\nseparate process connected to the `brok run` event bus, restricted to the\ntopics its manifest declares.","Shards are small programs that react to workspace events.","Shards are small programs that react to what happens in your workspace (a\nfile changed, a question was asked) and can publish their own events. The\nagent you installed is one.","Shards","Shard Hub (preview)","Shard Hub (prévia)","Seus primeiros minutos","Set up your first workspace","Semantic search loads the quantized model (~140 MB of weights) once per\nprocess. Run `brok run` and searches reuse its already-loaded model through\nthe bus instead of loading their own.","See Local LLM setup. Any OpenAI-compatible endpoint works:","Security","Search works without any LLM. Answers (`brok ask`, `chat`, `review`,\n`commit`) need one. A local model is free, private and works offline.","Search for `Qwen2.5-Coder-7B` (or the size from the table), pick a\n`Q4_K_M` or `Q5_K_M` file and download it.","Search","Runtime contract","Run `brok setup llm`: it finds the server and lets you pick the model.","Rules of thumb: library crates use `thiserror`/`anyhow::Result` with context\nand never print; only `brok-cli` talks to the terminal. Optional native\nbackends are cargo features, so the pure-Rust build always works.","reads your RAM (and NVIDIA GPU memory) and picks a model size from the\ntable below;","Prefer a hosted model for some questions? Export its key and choose it per\nrequest; the providers are preconfigured in `brok.yml`:","Prefer a graphical app? LM Studio works too: download a\nmodel, open **Developer / Local Server** and press **Start Server**. More in\nLocal LLM setup.","Precedence","Pick the model for your machine:","Pick a model that fits your machine and run it with Ollama or LM Studio.","Performance tips","Os fluxos de trabalho incluídos e como escrever e compartilhar os seus.","Os dois compartilham a mesma pasta `.brokspace/`, então você pode alternar a\nqualquer momento.","Option 2: LM Studio (graphical)","Option 1: Ollama (recommended, terminal friendly)","OpenAI-compatible chat completion endpoints used by `brok-agent`.","Open the **Developer / Local Server** tab, load the model and press\n**Start Server** (it listens on `http://localhost:1234`).","On `system:shutdown` (delivered without subscribing), exit within 3 seconds.","obtains the executable, in order of preference:","O que você ganha","O mesmo workspace em uma IDE feita em torno dele: uma página inicial que\ncomeça pela sua pergunta, o agente Brokspace no chat, busca, revisões e\nmensagens de commit a um clique.","O Hub está sendo construído. Até ele abrir, instale shards de qualquer\nrepositório git com `brok shard install <url>`.","O Brokspace Hub será o catálogo oficial de shards feitos pelo time do\nBrokspace e, mais tarde, um registro em que qualquer pessoa poderá publicar,\nno espírito do Docker Hub:","O Brokspace é código aberto (MIT ou Apache-2.0). Perguntas e ideias vão para\nas GitHub Discussions.","O Brokspace deixa qualquer workspace de desenvolvimento pesquisável e pronto para agentes, na sua máquina.","O Brokspace (`brok`) indexa seu código (um repositório, seus submódulos ou\numa pasta inteira de repositórios) em um mecanismo de busca híbrido local,\nconecta esse índice ao LLM que você escolher e o liga aos agentes de código\nque você já usa. Nada sai da sua máquina, a menos que você escolha um modelo\nhospedado.","O agente Brokspace","Nothing installed yet? It prints the one-line install for your OS. Run it,\nthen `brok setup llm` again. `brok doctor` tells you at any time whether the\nmodel is reachable.","Not sure? Skip the pull: `brok init` (next step) measures your machine and\noffers to download the right one.","Not sure where to start? Type `/ask-brok` in your coding agent and describe\nyour situation.","Na primeira vez, abra com clique direito > **Abrir** enquanto o app ainda\nnão é notarizado.","moves it into `.brokspace/shards/<name>/` and records the source, commit and\nbinary hash in `shards.lock`.","Model files are downloaded once per user and shared by every workspace:\n`~/.cache/brokspace/models` (Linux), `~/Library/Caches/brokspace/models`\n(macOS), `%LOCALAPPDATA%\\brokspace\\models` (Windows). Set `BROK_MODELS_DIR`\nto use another directory. A copy inside `.brokspace/cache/models/` (from\nolder versions) keeps working.","Memory profile","looks for a running **Ollama** (`localhost:11434`) or **LM Studio**\n(`localhost:1234`) server;","Local LLM setup","Local and hosted LLMs","Lifecycle","Keys are read from the environment, never stored in `brok.yml`, and secrets\nfound in retrieved code are redacted before any prompt leaves your machine.","It:","It walks through six steps and asks before anything big:","It detects your agents and, for each one, adds:","Introduction","Introdução","Integrations","Installing:","Installed with Cargo? Upgrade with `cargo install brok-cli brok-agent`.\nComing from brok 0.2.1 or older (no `upgrade` command yet)? Run the install\ncommand from step 1 again, once.","Install, set up your first workspace, use it every day: about 15 minutes.","Install brok","Install","Instale, configure seu primeiro workspace e use no dia a dia: cerca de 15\nminutos.","Instalação","Inside `brok chat`: `/skill grill-me` applies a skill to the conversation,\n`/clear` forgets it, `/exit` leaves.","Indexing streams files in batches; the Arrow store keeps staged batches in\nmemory until commit, LanceDB writes per batch.","Indexing pipeline","In any terminal and any editor. `brok search`, `ask`, `chat`, `review`,\n`commit`, skills and shards. Your coding agents get the `brok_search`\ntool through MCP.","If you skipped step 6 of `brok init`:","How it works","Hosted models","Hoje, crie os seus com Shards e\nSkills, começando pelo\ntemplate de shard.","Go to your project (one repository, or a folder holding several) and run\n(want a sample project first? clone\nexample-nestjs):","Getting started with Brokspace","Get a local LLM (optional)","From zero to a productive workspace in about 15 minutes. Each step is short;\nskip what you do not need.","From zero to a productive workspace in about 15 minutes.","Freshness: `brok-agent` reports dirty files every few seconds and, when a\nrepository's `HEAD` moves (commit, pull, checkout), the files that differ\nbetween the two commits; root, submodules and nested repositories alike.","For each partition: BM25 top-k and vector top-k (when the partition has\nvectors of the right size) → Reciprocal Rank Fusion (`k = 60`), normalized so\nthat rank 1 in every list scores 1.0. Partitions other than the focus (the\npartition of the current directory) are multiplied by `search.cold_weight`.\nThe final top-k chunk ids are materialized from their stores.","For each agent it does two things.","Existing entries in those files are preserved; only `brokspace` is added or\nupdated. When `brok run` is active, searches reuse its loaded model;\notherwise `brok mcp` opens the index read-only on demand.","Everything lives in **`.brokspace/brok.yml`**. Every key is optional and the\ndefaults are sensible. The settings people change most:","Everything is also in the **Brokspace** menu and the command palette:\nSet Up Workspace, Start / Stop / Restart, Rebuild Index, Doctor, Install,\nCreate and Remove Shard, Export Skills to Coding Agents, Run Skill, Review,\nWrite Commit Message. The status bar shows whether Brokspace is running and\nwhich model it uses.","Every shard lists the permissions it wants in `shard.json`, and you approve\nthem when installing. Guide: Shards.","Every request goes through `brok`, which sends it to the LLM set in\n`.brokspace/brok.yml` (Ollama, LM Studio or a hosted OpenAI-compatible API).\nWithout an LLM, or when it does not answer, the agent replies with what the\nlocal index found, as links.","Every line is either ✓, or a `!` with the exact command that fixes it.","Event bus","Escolha um modelo adequado à sua máquina e rode com Ollama ou LM Studio.","Environment variables","Em qualquer terminal e qualquer editor. `brok search`, `ask`, `chat`,\n`review`, `commit`, skills e shards. Seus agentes de código ganham a\nferramenta `brok_search` via MCP.","Editors and scripts: JSON output","Editors (the Brokspace IDE among them), scripts and CI read brok through\n`--json`. Shapes are stable within a minor version.","Easier ways to change things:","Each shard documents its own `settings`. For `brok-agent` see its\nREADME.","Duas formas de usar","Download the AppImage or the `.tar.gz` from the\nlatest release.","Download it from lmstudio.ai (Windows `.exe`,\nmacOS `.dmg` for Apple Silicon or Intel, Linux `.AppImage`:\n`chmod +x LM_Studio-*.AppImage && ./LM_Studio-*.AppImage`).","Download `BrokspaceIDE-<version>-windows-x64-setup.exe` from the\nlatest release. Choose\n**More info > Run anyway** in SmartScreen while the installer is not\nsigned yet.","Disable a shard without removing it in `brok.yml`:","Daemon lifecycle","Crie integrações que reagem ao seu workspace.","Credits","Crates and repositories","Crashing shards restart with exponential backoff (1 s … 30 s); five crashes\nwithin a minute and the supervisor gives up.","Connect your coding agent","Configure","Configuration reference","Como funciona","Commit these files and your whole team gets the same setup. In your agent,\nstart with `/ask-brok` and describe what you want to do.","Commit the generated files to give your whole team the same setup. `brok`\nmust be on `PATH` for agents to start `brok mcp`; `brok doctor` checks it.","Commands and languages","Comece","Comandos e idiomas","Coding agents","clones the repository (`--depth 1`, optional `--tag`) or uses the local directory;","Changes take effect on the next command (or after restarting brok run).","Changes take effect on the next command (or after restarting `brok run`).\nChanging `embeddings.model`, `embeddings.dimensions` or `index.store`\ntriggers a rebuild of the affected partitions on the next `brok index`.","Built-in skills","Built-in participants","Build integrations that react to your workspace.","Brokspace stays small and plugs into the tools you already use.","Brokspace makes any development workspace searchable and agent-ready, on your machine.","Brokspace is open source (MIT or Apache-2.0). Questions and ideas go to\nGitHub Discussions.","Brokspace IDE is built on Eclipse Theia, so VS\nCode extensions from Open VSX work in it. It ships\nwith `brok` and `brok-agent`, and puts them on your `PATH`.","Brokspace IDE","Brokspace answers questions (brok ask) and runs skills (brok skill run) with any OpenAI-compatible model.","Brokspace answers questions (`brok ask`) and runs skills (`brok skill run`)\nwith any OpenAI-compatible model. Running it locally keeps everything\n**free, private and offline**. Search and indexing never need an LLM.","Brokspace (`brok`) indexes your code (one repository, its submodules, or a\nwhole folder of repositories) into a local hybrid search engine, connects it\nto the LLM you choose, and plugs it into the coding agents you already use.\nNothing leaves your machine unless you choose a hosted model.","Both stores share one Arrow schema (`brok-index/src/schema.rs`): `id`, `path`,\n`language`, `kind`, `symbol`, `parent`, `signature`, line and byte ranges,\n`file_hash`, `content` and an optional `FixedSizeList<Float32>` `vector`.","Both share the same `.brokspace/` folder, so you can switch at any time.","Both install two programs, `brok` and `brok-agent`, and check their\nchecksums. Open a new terminal and check:","Baixe o AppImage ou o `.tar.gz` da\nversão mais recente.","Baixe `BrokspaceIDE-<versão>-windows-x64-setup.exe` da\nversão mais recente.\nNo SmartScreen, escolha **Mais informações > Executar assim mesmo**\nenquanto o instalador ainda não é assinado.","Architecture","An IDE with Brokspace built in, for IDE mode next to the brok CLI.","an environment containing only OS basics (`PATH`, `HOME`, `TEMP`, …),\n`RUST_LOG`, the variables allowed by `permissions.env`, and:","an `entrypoint` already present in the repository;","After editing `brok.yml`, run `brok restart`. Every key is explained in\nConfiguration reference.","A workspace skill with the same name as a built-in one replaces it, so you\ncan tailor any built-in to your team. More in Skills.","A visão Brokspace","A skill is a small, reusable workflow written for AI agents: a folder with a SKILL.md (YAML frontmatter name + description, then instructions) and optional reference files.","A skill is a small, reusable workflow for AI: a `SKILL.md` file with\ninstructions. Brokspace ships 20 of them.","A shard can also ship skills next to its process (`entrypoint` + `skills`).","a release asset for this platform, verified against its SHA-256;","A non-zero exit is a crash: the shard is restarted with backoff.","A janela começa enxuta: Explorer, Busca, Controle de Código-Fonte e Brokspace\nà esquerda, e o **agente Brokspace** fixo à direita. Depuração, Testes e\nExtensões ficam a um atalho de distância.","A IDE se atualiza sozinha pelo GitHub Releases. Para receber respostas\nescritas você precisa de um LLM: veja LLM local (a\nbusca funciona sem ele).","A IDE está em inglês e em português do Brasil. Ela começa em português em um\nsistema em português; troque em **Idioma** na página inicial.","A IDE conversa com o Brokspace apenas pela CLI `brok` e sua saída JSON (veja\nIntegrações), então ela mostra exatamente o que o\n`brok` vê, e tudo o que ela faz você também pode fazer em um terminal. Ela\nprecisa do brok 0.2.4 ou mais recente; o que vem com ela atende.","A failure ends the stream with a non-zero exit code and the message on\nstderr. Follow-up questions pass the conversation so far:\n`brok ask --json --history turns.json \"and where is it tested?\"`, where\n`turns.json` holds `[{\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": \"...\"}, {\"role\":\n\"assistant\", \"content\": \"...\"}]`.","A casa oficial de shards, skills e agentes para o Brokspace.","A Brokspace IDE é feita sobre o Eclipse Theia,\nentão extensões do VS Code do Open VSX funcionam\nnela. Ela já vem com o `brok` e o `brok-agent` e os coloca no seu `PATH`.","A **skill** is a small, reusable workflow written for AI agents: a folder\nwith a `SKILL.md` (YAML frontmatter `name` + `description`, then\ninstructions) and optional reference files. Brokspace uses the same\nAgent Skills format as Claude Code,\nCodex, Cursor and GitHub Copilot, so a skill written once works everywhere.","A **skill shard** is a shard with no process, just skills. Publish it as a\ngit repository and anyone can install it:","a **search tool** (`brok_search`) through MCP, so the agent finds code by\nmeaning before grepping;","9. Troubleshooting","8. Shards","7. Skills","6. Configure","5. Connect your coding agent","4. Use it every day","3. Set up your first workspace","2. Get a local LLM (optional)","11. Uninstall","10. Update brok","1. Install brok","¹ A shard needs an `entrypoint`, `skills`, or both. Skill-only shards run no\nprocess, so they cannot declare topics, `build` or `releases`.","| Your machine | Model                | Download                         |\n| ------------ | -------------------- | -------------------------------- |\n| 8 GB         | `qwen2.5-coder:1.5b` | `ollama pull qwen2.5-coder:1.5b` |","| Your machine                          | Model              | Download                       |\n| ------------------------------------- | ------------------ | ------------------------------ |\n| 16 GB, no GPU (most business laptops) | `qwen2.5-coder:3b` | `ollama pull qwen2.5-coder:3b` |","| Your machine                                            | Model               | Download                        |\n| ------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------- | ------------------------------- |\n| A GPU with 12 GB+, or 32 GB with a GPU or Apple Silicon | `qwen2.5-coder:14b` | `ollama pull qwen2.5-coder:14b` |","| Your machine                                                   | Model              | Download                       |\n| -------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------ | ------------------------------ |\n| 16 GB with a GPU (6 GB+) or Apple Silicon; 32 GB without a GPU | `qwen2.5-coder:7b` | `ollama pull qwen2.5-coder:7b` |","| You want to... | Run                                                               |\n| -------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Tab completion | `brok completions bash >> ~/.bashrc` (also zsh, fish, powershell) |","| You want to...      | Run           |\n| ------------------- | ------------- |\n| See what is indexed | `brok status` |","| You want to...       | Run            |\n| -------------------- | -------------- |\n| See what it is doing | `brok logs -f` |","| You want to...              | Run                   |\n| --------------------------- | --------------------- |\n| Just print a commit message | `brok commit --print` |","| You want to...                 | Run                    |\n| ------------------------------ | ---------------------- |\n| Rebuild the index from scratch | `brok index --rebuild` |","| You want to...                      | Run            |\n| ----------------------------------- | -------------- |\n| Restart it after editing `brok.yml` | `brok restart` |","| You want to...                      | Run                        |\n| ----------------------------------- | -------------------------- |\n| Start / stop the background service | `brok start` / `brok stop` |","| You want to...                         | Run                           |\n| -------------------------------------- | ----------------------------- |\n| Use a different model for one question | `brok ask -p anthropic \"...\"` |","| You want to...                          | Run                                   |\n| --------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------- |\n| Show whole results, or JSON for scripts | `brok search \"...\" --full` / `--json` |","| You want to...                          | Run                                                |\n| --------------------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------- |\n| Review only staged changes, or a branch | `brok review --staged` / `brok review --base main` |","| Variable   | Used by | Purpose         |\n| ---------- | ------- | --------------- |\n| `NO_COLOR` | CLI     | Disable colors. |","| Variable   | Used by | Purpose                                       |\n| ---------- | ------- | --------------------------------------------- |\n| `RUST_LOG` | all     | Log filter, e.g. `RUST_LOG=brok_index=debug`. |","| Variable     | Value                              |\n| ------------ | ---------------------------------- |\n| `BROK_TOKEN` | The shard's session token (secret) |","| Variable       | Value      |\n| -------------- | ---------- |\n| `BROK_NETWORK` | `1` or `0` |","| Variable        | Value                              |\n| --------------- | ---------------------------------- |\n| `BROK_ENDPOINT` | Socket path / pipe name of the bus |","| Variable         | Value                   |\n| ---------------- | ----------------------- |\n| `BROK_WORKSPACE` | Absolute workspace root |","| Variable          | Value         |\n| ----------------- | ------------- |\n| `BROK_SHARD_NAME` | Manifest name |","| Variable          | Used by | Purpose                                          |\n| ----------------- | ------- | ------------------------------------------------ |\n| `BROK_*` (others) | shards  | Set by `brok run` for shard processes; reserved. |","| Variable          | Used by | Purpose                                                  |\n| ----------------- | ------- | -------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `BROK_MODELS_DIR` | CLI     | Embedding model cache (default: the OS cache directory). |","| Variable          | Used by | Purpose                                                     |\n| ----------------- | ------- | ----------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `BROK_CONFIG_DIR` | CLI     | User defaults directory (default: the OS config directory). |","| Variable                         | Value                         |\n| -------------------------------- | ----------------------------- |\n| `BROK_FS_READ` / `BROK_FS_WRITE` | Declared paths, `;`-separated |","| Type      | It runs                              |\n| --------- | ------------------------------------ |\n| `/review` | A review of your uncommitted changes |","| Type       | It runs                                 |\n| ---------- | --------------------------------------- |\n| A question | `brok ask` with the conversation so far |","| Type             | It runs                        |\n| ---------------- | ------------------------------ |\n| `/review staged` | A review of the staged changes |","| Type                 | It runs                                 |\n| -------------------- | --------------------------------------- |\n| `/review base <ref>` | A review of this branch against `<ref>` |","| Type                    | It runs                                                     |\n| ----------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `/skill <name> <input>` | A skill on your LLM, e.g. `/skill tdd add a priority field` |","| Topic       | Payload                                | Direction   |\n| ----------- | -------------------------------------- | ----------- |\n| `agent:ask` | `{prompt, provider?, context_chunks?}` | CLI → agent |","| Topic          | Payload                              | Direction                  |\n| -------------- | ------------------------------------ | -------------------------- |\n| `file:changed` | `{changed: [path], deleted: [path]}` | agent → index (and anyone) |","| Topic           | Payload             | Direction      |\n| --------------- | ------------------- | -------------- |\n| `index:updated` | counts and duration | index → anyone |","| Topic           | Payload                    | Direction      |\n| --------------- | -------------------------- | -------------- |\n| `review:result` | `{path, verdict, summary}` | agent → anyone |","| Topic             | Payload    | Direction          |\n| ----------------- | ---------- | ------------------ |\n| `system:shutdown` | `{reason}` | runtime → everyone |","| Topic                                  | Payload        | Direction         |\n| -------------------------------------- | -------------- | ----------------- |\n| `agent:ask.chunk` / `.done` / `.error` | streamed reply | agent → requester |","| Topic                                  | Payload                           | Direction     |\n| -------------------------------------- | --------------------------------- | ------------- |\n| `index:search` / `index:search.result` | `SearchRequest` / `SearchResults` | request/reply |","| Tool          | What it does                                     |\n| ------------- | ------------------------------------------------ |\n| `brok_status` | What is indexed and whether `brok run` is active |","| Tool          | What it does                                                                              |\n| ------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `brok_search` | Hybrid search over the local index; returns whole functions/classes with `path:start-end` |","| Symptom              | Fix                                                                                                                                                                                                                                 |\n| -------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Answers take minutes | The model runs on your CPU. Normal for 7b on a laptop without a GPU (a review can take 3 to 5 minutes); for faster answers use 3b: `ollama pull qwen2.5-coder:3b`, then `brok setup llm --provider ollama --model qwen2.5-coder:3b` |","| Symptom                   | Fix                                                              |\n| ------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Search misses recent code | `brok status`; if the daemon is stopped, `brok start` catches up |","| Symptom                    | Fix                                                          |\n| -------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `no answer from the agent` | Start your LLM (open Ollama / LM Studio), then `brok doctor` |","| Symptom                       | Fix                                             |\n| ----------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------- |\n| `ollama ... is not installed` | `ollama pull <model>` as shown by `brok doctor` |","| Symptom                       | Fix                                                    |\n| ----------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------ |\n| Odd behavior after an upgrade | `brok restart`; if it persists, `brok index --rebuild` |","| Symptom                        | Fix                                                |\n| ------------------------------ | -------------------------------------------------- |\n| Results come back as text only | The search model is missing: `brok model download` |","| Symptom                          | Fix                                                                         |\n| -------------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Windows: errors about long paths | Enable long paths (`brok doctor` shows the command) or use a shorter folder |","| Symptom                            | Fix                                                                     |\n| ---------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Agent does not show the brok tools | `brok` must be on `PATH`; run `brok setup agents` and restart the agent |","| Symptom                                     | Fix                                                                                                      |\n| ------------------------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `another brok process is writing the index` | `brok` is running in the background and already indexes for you; skip `brok index`, or `brok stop` first |","| Step     | What happens                                                      |\n| -------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| 5. Index | Indexes your code (functions, classes and sections, not raw text) |","| Step     | What happens                                                               |\n| -------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| 2. Agent | Installs `brok-agent`, the helper that tracks changes and talks to the LLM |","| Step         | What happens                                      |\n| ------------ | ------------------------------------------------- |\n| 1. Workspace | Creates `.brokspace/` with a commented `brok.yml` |","| Step         | What happens                                                      |\n| ------------ | ----------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| 4. Local LLM | Finds Ollama / LM Studio and picks a model that fits your machine |","| Step             | What happens                                                          |\n| ---------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| 6. Coding agents | Connects Claude Code, Cursor, VS Code or Codex (skills + search tool) |","| Step               | What happens                                                           |\n| ------------------ | ---------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| 3. Semantic search | Downloads the search model once (~140 MB, shared by all your projects) |","| Section    | What it shows                                                      |\n| ---------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| **Skills** | Workflows you run and the skills your agents use; click to run one |","| Section    | What it shows                                                                                                                                                                                                                                        |\n| ---------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| **Shards** | Each installed shard and its state; expand one to see what it reads and writes, whether it uses the network, the programs it runs, the events it listens to and publishes, and where it came from. Install, create or remove shards from the toolbar |","| Section      | What it shows                                                                         |\n| ------------ | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| **Overview** | Whether Brokspace is running, the model, the index, search, and Ask / Review / Commit |","| Seção      | O que mostra                                                                                |\n| ---------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| **Skills** | Fluxos de trabalho que você executa e as skills que seus agentes usam; clique para executar |","| Seção      | O que mostra                                                                                                                                                                                                                      |\n| ---------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| **Shards** | Cada shard instalado e seu estado; expanda um para ver o que ele lê e escreve, se usa a rede, os programas que executa, os eventos que escuta e publica, e de onde veio. Instale, crie ou remova shards pela barra de ferramentas |","| Seção           | O que mostra                                                                            |\n| --------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| **Visão Geral** | Se o Brokspace está rodando, o modelo, o índice, a busca e Perguntar / Revisar / Commit |","| Participant | Identity            | Publishes      | Subscribes      |\n| ----------- | ------------------- | -------------- | --------------- |\n| Shards      | their manifest name | `publishes_to` | `subscribes_to` |","| Participant   | Identity     | Publishes | Subscribes                     |\n| ------------- | ------------ | --------- | ------------------------------ |\n| Index service | `brok-index` | `index:*` | `file:changed`, `index:search` |","| Participant                                 | Identity   | Publishes            | Subscribes |\n| ------------------------------------------- | ---------- | -------------------- | ---------- |\n| CLI (`brok ask`, `brok bus`, `brok search`) | `operator` | any non-system topic | `*`        |","| OS    | Install               |\n| ----- | --------------------- |\n| macOS | `brew install ollama` |","| OS    | Install                                          |\n| ----- | ------------------------------------------------ |\n| macOS | `brew install ollama` or the app from ollama.com |","| OS    | Install                                          |\n| ----- | ------------------------------------------------ |\n| Linux | `curl -fsSL https://ollama.com/install.sh \\| sh` |","| OS      | Install                        |\n| ------- | ------------------------------ |\n| Windows | `winget install Ollama.Ollama` |","| OS      | Install                                                         |\n| ------- | --------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Windows | `winget install Ollama.Ollama` or the installer from ollama.com |","| Model size | Memory and GPU | Typical hardware                 | Recommended (Ollama)                |\n| ---------- | -------------- | -------------------------------- | ----------------------------------- |\n| 1B to 3B   | 8 GB           | Office laptops, entry-level Macs | `qwen2.5-coder:1.5b`, `llama3.2:3b` |","| Model size | Memory and GPU | Typical hardware                          | Recommended (Ollama)              |\n| ---------- | -------------- | ----------------------------------------- | --------------------------------- |\n| 3B         | 16 GB, no GPU  | Business laptops with integrated graphics | `qwen2.5-coder:3b`, `llama3.2:3b` |","| Model size | Memory and GPU                                          | Typical hardware                      | Recommended (Ollama)                   |\n| ---------- | ------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------- | -------------------------------------- |\n| 14B to 32B | A GPU with 12 GB+, or 32 GB with a GPU or Apple Silicon | Workstations, Mac Pro/Max with 32 GB+ | `qwen2.5-coder:14b`, `deepseek-r1:32b` |","| Model size                | Memory and GPU                                                 | Typical hardware                        | Recommended (Ollama)                              |\n| ------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------- | --------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------- |\n| **7B to 9B** (sweet spot) | 16 GB with a GPU (6 GB+) or Apple Silicon; 32 GB without a GPU | Gaming laptops, M1/M2/M3 Macs, desktops | `qwen2.5-coder:7b`, `llama3:8b`, `deepseek-r1:8b` |","| Key     | Default | Description                |\n| ------- | ------- | -------------------------- |\n| `limit` | `8`     | Default number of results. |","| Key     | Default | Description                                                                                             |\n| ------- | ------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `store` | `auto`  | `auto` (LanceDB when compiled in), `lancedb` or `arrow` (memory-mapped Arrow IPC, exact vector search). |","| Key     | Default                 | Description                     |\n| ------- | ----------------------- | ------------------------------- |\n| `model` | `nomic-embed-text-v1.5` | The only supported model today. |","| Key      | Default | Description                                                                                |\n| -------- | ------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `device` | `auto`  | `auto`, `cpu`, `cuda`, `coreml`, `directml` (GPU devices need the matching build feature). |","| Key       | Description                               |\n| --------- | ----------------------------------------- |\n| `backend` | `none`, `s3`, `r2`, `minio` or `git-lfs`. |","| Key       | Description                                                                           |\n| --------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `default` | Provider used unless `brok ask --provider` says otherwise. Must exist in `providers`. |","| Key       | Default | Description                                                         |\n| --------- | ------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `enabled` | `true`  | `false` runs on BM25 text search only: no download, minimal memory. |","| Key       | Default    | Description                                               |\n| --------- | ---------- | --------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `include` | `[\"**/*\"]` | Globs (relative to the workspace root) of files to index. |","| Key       | Default     | Description                                            |\n| --------- | ----------- | ------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `variant` | `quantized` | `quantized` (~140 MB, int8) or `full` (~550 MB, fp32). |","| Key       | Default                                                                                                                                                                    | Description                                                          |\n| --------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `exclude` | `.git`, `.brokspace`, `target`, `node_modules`, `dist`, `build`, lock files (`*.lock`, `pnpm-lock.yaml`, `package-lock.json`, `npm-shrinkwrap.json`, `go.sum`), `*.min.js` | Globs to skip. `.gitignore` files are always honored on top of this. |","| Key          | Default | Description                |\n| ------------ | ------- | -------------------------- |\n| `batch_size` | `16`    | Texts per inference batch. |","| Key          | Default | Description                                                |\n| ------------ | ------- | ---------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `dimensions` | `768`   | Matryoshka truncation: `64`, `128`, `256`, `512` or `768`. |","| Key          | Default | Description                                                                                                                                 |\n| ------------ | ------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `submodules` | `true`  | Index git submodules and git repositories nested in the workspace (up to 4 levels, e.g. a folder of repos) as independent _hot_ partitions. |","| Key           | Default | Description                                                                  |\n| ------------- | ------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `cold_weight` | `0.85`  | Score multiplier for partitions other than the one you run the command from. |","| Key           | Default | Description                                                                                |\n| ------------- | ------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `max_file_kb` | `512`   | Larger files are skipped. Binary files (NUL bytes) and non UTF-8 files are always skipped. |","| Key               | Default | Description                                                                                          |\n| ----------------- | ------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `max_chunk_lines` | `120`   | A syntactic unit longer than this is split: containers into members, other nodes at line boundaries. |","| Key                      | Description                            |\n| ------------------------ | -------------------------------------- |\n| `providers.<name>.model` | Model name as the provider expects it. |","| Key                         | Description                    |\n| --------------------------- | ------------------------------ |\n| `providers.<name>.base_url` | URL up to and including `/v1`. |","| Key                            | Description                                                                       |\n| ------------------------------ | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `providers.<name>.api_key_env` | **Name** of the environment variable holding the key. Keys never go in this file. |","| Key                                        | Description                                                                                             |\n| ------------------------------------------ | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `remote.access_key_env` / `secret_key_env` | Names of the variables holding the credentials (default `AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID` / `AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY`). |","| Key                                           | Description                 |\n| --------------------------------------------- | --------------------------- |\n| `providers.<name>.temperature` / `max_tokens` | Optional sampling settings. |","| Key                                                | Description                 |\n| -------------------------------------------------- | --------------------------- |\n| `remote.bucket` / `prefix` / `region` / `endpoint` | Object storage coordinates. |","| Integration   | How           | Setup            |\n| ------------- | ------------- | ---------------- |\n| Anything else | write a shard | `brok shard new` |","| Integration        | How                                  | Setup     |\n| ------------------ | ------------------------------------ | --------- |\n| Git and submodules | change tracking, hot/cold partitions | automatic |","| Integration                    | How                   | Setup            |\n| ------------------------------ | --------------------- | ---------------- |\n| Local LLMs (Ollama, LM Studio) | OpenAI-compatible API | `brok setup llm` |","| Integration                           | How             | Setup             |\n| ------------------------------------- | --------------- | ----------------- |\n| Team storage (S3, R2, MinIO, Git LFS) | index mirroring | `brok setup sync` |","| Integration                                              | How                           | Setup              |\n| -------------------------------------------------------- | ----------------------------- | ------------------ |\n| Hosted LLMs (Anthropic, DeepSeek, any OpenAI-compatible) | `llm.providers` in `brok.yml` | export the API key |","| Integration                                                   | How                | Setup               |\n| ------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------ | ------------------- |\n| Coding agents (Claude Code, Cursor, VS Code / Copilot, Codex) | MCP tools + skills | `brok setup agents` |","| Field  | Required | Rules                                     |\n| ------ | -------- | ----------------------------------------- |\n| `brok` |          | SemVer requirement on the runtime version |","| Field  | Required | Rules                                             |\n| ------ | -------- | ------------------------------------------------- |\n| `name` | ✓        | `^[a-z][a-z0-9-]{1,63}$`, unique in the workspace |","| Field    | Required | Rules                                                        |\n| -------- | -------- | ------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `skills` | ✓¹       | Directories whose subfolders each hold a `SKILL.md` (skills) |","| Field     | Required | Rules  |\n| --------- | -------- | ------ |\n| `version` | ✓        | SemVer |","| Field     | Required | Rules              |\n| --------- | -------- | ------------------ |\n| `runtime` |          | `native` (default) |","| Field        | Required | Rules                                                                   |\n| ------------ | -------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `entrypoint` | ✓¹       | Relative path inside the shard directory; `.exe` is appended on Windows |","| Field           | Required | Rules                                             |\n| --------------- | -------- | ------------------------------------------------- |\n| `build.command` |          | Program + arguments, executed **without a shell** |","| Field             | Required | Rules                                                                                  |\n| ----------------- | -------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `permissions.env` |          | Variables to pass through: exact names, `PREFIX_*` or `*_SUFFIX`. `BROK_*` is reserved |","| Field                 | Required | Rules              |\n| --------------------- | -------- | ------------------ |\n| `permissions.network` |          | `false` by default |","| Field                 | Required | Rules                                       |\n| --------------------- | -------- | ------------------------------------------- |\n| `permissions.process` |          | Bare program names the shard intends to run |","| Field                  | Required | Rules                                                                                                                              |\n| ---------------------- | -------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `releases.<os>-<arch>` |          | `https://` URL and 64 hex SHA-256; keys use Rust's `std::env::consts` names (`linux-x86_64`, `macos-aarch64`, `windows-x86_64`, …) |","| Field                            | Required | Rules                                                            |\n| -------------------------------- | -------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `subscribes_to` / `publishes_to` |          | Topic patterns; publishing to `system:*` (or `*`) is not allowed |","| Field                               | Required | Rules                                                |\n| ----------------------------------- | -------- | ---------------------------------------------------- |\n| `permissions.filesystem.read/write` |          | Workspace relative paths, no `..`, no absolute paths |","| Digite    | Ele executa                                    |\n| --------- | ---------------------------------------------- |\n| `/review` | Uma revisão das suas alterações não commitadas |","| Digite       | Ele executa                        |\n| ------------ | ---------------------------------- |\n| Uma pergunta | `brok ask` com a conversa até aqui |","| Digite           | Ele executa                           |\n| ---------------- | ------------------------------------- |\n| `/review staged` | Uma revisão das alterações preparadas |","| Digite               | Ele executa                                   |\n| -------------------- | --------------------------------------------- |\n| `/review base <ref>` | Uma revisão deste branch em relação a `<ref>` |","| Digite                    | Ele executa                                                                     |\n| ------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `/skill <nome> <entrada>` | Uma skill no seu LLM, por exemplo `/skill tdd adicionar um campo de prioridade` |","| Command              | Output                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                      |\n| -------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `brok status --json` | One document: `version`, `initialized`, `root`, `daemon.running`, `backends`, `embeddings`, `llm` (`provider`, `model`, `base_url`), `index[]` (`tier`, `path`, `files`, `chunks`, `backend`, `semantic`), `shards[]` (`name`, `version`, `description`, `state`, `source`). Outside a workspace: `{\"version\": ..., \"initialized\": false}`. |","| Command                  | Output                                                                          |\n| ------------------------ | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `brok skill list --json` | One array: `name`, `description`, `user_invoked`, `source`, `bucket` per skill. |","| Command                      | Output                                                                                              |\n| ---------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `brok search <query> --json` | One document: `hits[]` with `path`, `start_line`, `end_line`, `kind`, `symbol`, `score`, `content`. |","| Command                                                                  | Output                                         |\n| ------------------------------------------------------------------------ | ---------------------------------------------- |\n| `brok ask ... --json`, `brok review --json`, `brok skill run ... --json` | A stream, one JSON event per line (see below). |","| Change                     | Command             |\n| -------------------------- | ------------------- |\n| Connect more coding agents | `brok setup agents` |","| Change                        | Command                                                                    |\n| ----------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Switch the local LLM or model | `brok setup llm` (or `brok setup llm --provider ollama --model llama3:8b`) |","| Change                                   | Command           |\n| ---------------------------------------- | ----------------- |\n| Share the index (Git LFS, S3, R2, MinIO) | `brok setup sync` |","| Agent | Files written                                                       |\n| ----- | ------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Codex | `.agents/skills/` (prints the MCP lines for `~/.codex/config.toml`) |","| Agent | File written                                  |\n| ----- | --------------------------------------------- |\n| Codex | prints the snippet for `~/.codex/config.toml` |","| Agent  | Files written                         |\n| ------ | ------------------------------------- |\n| Cursor | `.cursor/mcp.json`, `.agents/skills/` |","| Agent  | File written                                |\n| ------ | ------------------------------------------- |\n| Cursor | `.cursor/mcp.json` (`mcpServers.brokspace`) |","| Agent       | Files written                  |\n| ----------- | ------------------------------ |\n| Claude Code | `.mcp.json`, `.claude/skills/` |","| Agent       | File written                         |\n| ----------- | ------------------------------------ |\n| Claude Code | `.mcp.json` (`mcpServers.brokspace`) |","| Agent             | Files written                         |\n| ----------------- | ------------------------------------- |\n| VS Code / Copilot | `.vscode/mcp.json`, `.agents/skills/` |","| Agent             | File written                             |\n| ----------------- | ---------------------------------------- |\n| VS Code / Copilot | `.vscode/mcp.json` (`servers.brokspace`) |","|      | User-invoked                                | Model-invoked                                |\n| ---- | ------------------------------------------- | -------------------------------------------- |\n| Role | Orchestrates a flow (`/to-spec`, `/triage`) | A reusable discipline (`tdd`, `code-review`) |","|             | User-invoked          | Model-invoked               |\n| ----------- | --------------------- | --------------------------- |\n| Description | One human-facing line | Rich \"Use when...\" triggers |","|             | User-invoked                     | Model-invoked |\n| ----------- | -------------------------------- | ------------- |\n| Frontmatter | `disable-model-invocation: true` | (default)     |","|               | User-invoked                | Model-invoked                        |\n| ------------- | --------------------------- | ------------------------------------ |\n| Who starts it | Only you, by typing `/name` | You, or the agent when the task fits |","> Your next project is faster: the search model and your LLM choice are\n> remembered, so `brok init` there takes seconds.","`workspace`","`sync`","`shards`","`shard.json` of a skill shard:","`shard.json`","`search`","`namespace:name`, lowercase letters, digits, `-`, `_` and `.` for sub-topics:\n`file:changed`, `agent:ask.chunk`. Patterns are exact topics or a prefix\nending in `*` (`agent:ask.*`, `file:*`, `*`). Pick a namespace named after\nyour shard for your own events. The well-known topics and their payloads are\nlisted in Architecture.","`llm`","`index`","`git-lfs` tracks `.brokspace/databases/**` with Git LFS and stops ignoring it,\nso the index travels with the repository. The object storage sync engine\n(`brok sync`) is on the roadmap: today `brok setup sync` records the target.","`embeddings`","`client.request(event)` returns a stream of replies; `client.call::<Req,\nRes>(&req, timeout)` waits for the first typed reply. Example: query the\nindex with `client.call::<SearchRequest, SearchResults>(…)` (add\n`index:search` to `publishes_to`).","`client.reply(&request, &payload)` answers a request; only the requester\nreceives it.","`client.context()` returns the workspace root, your `shards.<name>.settings`\nfrom `brok.yml` and the `llm` routing table.","`brok` ships a curated set, embedded in the binary (source:\nskills/). They cover the whole development loop that\nBrokspace itself uses: align, specify, slice, build test-first, review, ship.","`brok upgrade` downloads the new `brok` and `brok-agent`, checks them\nagainst the release checksums, swaps them in and restarts brok in every\nworkspace where it was running (each workspace's agent is refreshed on\nthat restart). `brok doctor` tells you when a new version is out.","`brok setup llm` applies exactly this table. Override it any time:","`brok setup llm` also stores your LLM choice in the user configuration\n(`~/.config/brokspace/config.yml`, `~/Library/Application Support/brokspace/`\nor `%APPDATA%\\brokspace\\`; override with `BROK_CONFIG_DIR`). `brok init`\napplies it to every new workspace, so you choose a model once per machine.","`brok run` starts the entrypoint with:","`brok run` is the daemon in the foreground; `brok start` launches the same\nprocess detached (output in `.brokspace/logs/brok.log`), and `brok ask`,\n`chat`, `review`, `commit` and `skill run` start it on demand. Readiness means\nthe bus is listening and, when installed, `brok-agent` is connected; the CLI\nchecks it with a `daemon:status` request.","`brok init` writes `.brokspace/brok.yml` with comments (commands that change\nthe file, like `brok setup llm`, keep them; comments you add yourself are\ndropped when brok rewrites the file). Every key is optional;\nmissing keys take the defaults below. Unknown keys are rejected with a\n\"did you mean\" style error, so typos never go unnoticed.","`brok index` and `brok run` take an exclusive OS file lock on\n`databases/.lock`; readers (`brok search`, `brok status`) never block.","**Write**: delete the file's previous chunks, append the new ones, update\nBM25 and the manifest, then commit atomically. Files are processed in\nbatches of 512 so memory stays bounded on large repositories.","**Windows (PowerShell)**","**Walk** with the `ignore` crate (nested `.gitignore`s, global excludes),\nthen apply `index.include` / `index.exclude`.","**User-invoked** skills are started by you (type `/name` in your agent, e.g.\n`/grill-me` before a big change). **Model-invoked** skills are picked by the\nagent when the task fits (e.g. `tdd`, `code-review`).","**Transport**: Unix domain socket at `.brokspace/run/brok.sock` (falls back\nto `$XDG_RUNTIME_DIR` for long paths) or the named pipe\n`\\\\.\\pipe\\brok-<hash of the workspace path>`. Frames are a 4-byte big-endian\nlength plus JSON, capped at 16 MiB.","**Storage**: keep models on an SSD; loading from a spinning disk is painfully slow.","**Smaller is often better** for interactive use: a fast 7B beats a slow\n14B for everyday questions; switch per request with `-p`.","**Skip unchanged files** cheaply: same size and mtime as in `files.json` →\nuntouched; otherwise hash the content and compare.","**Skills:** 20 fluxos de trabalho para IA já incluídos (TDD, code review,\nespecificações...) e os seus próprios em um `SKILL.md`.","**Skills:** 20 built-in workflows for AI (TDD, code review, specs...), and\nyour own in a `SKILL.md`.","**shows the requested capabilities and asks for consent** (`--yes` to skip in scripts);","**Shards:** small programs that react to your workspace through a local,\npermissioned event bus.","**Shards:** pequenos programas que reagem ao seu workspace por meio de um\nbarramento de eventos local e com permissões.","**Shards e pacotes de skills oficiais**, revisados e versionados.","**Semantics**: topic patterns (`file:*`), `source` stamped by the bus,\n`system:*` reserved and broadcast, request/reply via `correlation_id` routed\nonly to the requester (a bounded table with a 15 minute TTL).","**Search.** The Brokspace view (the folded \"B\" in the activity bar) finds\ncode by meaning or by name; click a result to open it.","**Search that understands code.** Functions, classes and sections are\nindexed whole, found by meaning or by name, across every repository.","**Router**: a single actor task owns all state, so routing is lock-free.\nDelivery uses bounded queues and `try_send`: a slow client loses events (and\nis logged) rather than stalling everyone.","**Route** each file to the deepest partition containing it\n(`PartitionMap::resolve`).","**Revisões e mensagens de commit** a partir das suas alterações preparadas\nou não commitadas.","**Revise e faça commit.** Digite `/review` no chat (ou `/review staged`,\n`/review base main`). No Controle de Código-Fonte, o botão ✨ escreve a\nmensagem de commit a partir das alterações preparadas.","**Reviews and commit messages** from your staged or uncommitted changes.","**Review and commit.** Type `/review` in the chat (or `/review staged`,\n`/review base main`). In Source Control, the ✨ button writes the commit\nmessage from the staged changes.","**Respostas com fontes.** Pergunte ao seu próprio LLM (Ollama, LM Studio ou\num modelo hospedado) sobre o workspace; toda resposta lista o código usado.","**Prefer Cargo?** `cargo install brok-cli brok-agent` (needs a C compiler and\n`protoc`), or `cargo install brok-cli brok-agent --no-default-features` for a\nlighter build with text search only.","**Permissões às claras:** cada shard lista o que pode ler, escrever,\nexecutar e acessar antes de você instalá-lo.","**Permissions up front:** every shard lists what it may read, write, run\nand reach, before you install it.","**Pergunte.** Digite uma pergunta na página inicial ou no painel do\nagente: o agente Brokspace responde com o seu LLM e cita as fontes usadas;\nclique em uma fonte para abrir o arquivo naquela linha. Perguntas de\nacompanhamento mantêm a conversa. Pressione `Ctrl+Shift+A`\n(`Cmd+Shift+A` no macOS) para o **modo foco no agente**, em que o agente\nocupa a maior parte da janela.","**Open a folder** (File > Open Folder). If it has no Brokspace workspace\nyet, the Brokspace view offers **Set Up Workspace**: it runs `brok init`\nfor you.","**One-command install** from the CLI and from the Brokspace IDE.","**On your local LLM**, through `brok-agent` (needs `brok run`):","**Ollama** (recommended):","**Official shards and skill packs**, reviewed and versioned.","**NVIDIA / AMD GPUs**: enable full GPU offload in LM Studio or Ollama.","**macOS / Linux**","**LanceDB**: deletes/appends go straight to the table; compaction runs every\n16 writes and an ANN index is built past 10 000 rows.","**Instalação com um comando** pela CLI e pela Brokspace IDE.","**In your coding agent** (the main way):","**Handshake**: `Hello{protocol, name, version, token}` → `Welcome{session,\nidentity, context}` or `Error`. Tokens are 256-bit random, stored hashed.","**Embed** in batches on a blocking thread (`spawn_blocking`), prefixing\n`search_document:` as nomic models expect; mean pooling → layer norm →\nMatryoshka truncation → L2 normalization.","**Company laptop blocks the script?** Download `brok-windows-x86_64.exe`\nfrom the brok release\nand `brok-agent-windows-x86_64.exe` from the\nagent release,\nrename them `brok.exe` and `brok-agent.exe`, put both in one folder and add\nthat folder to your `PATH`.","**Coding agents** (Claude Code, Cursor, VS Code, Codex): `brok setup agents`\ngives them the Brokspace search tool and skills; see\nIntegrations.","**Chunk** in parallel (rayon). The AST chunker emits one chunk per\ndefinition, attaches doc comments/attributes/decorators, splits large\ncontainers into a header plus members (`parent` = the container) and\ngroups loose top-level code into `preamble` chunks.","**Busque.** A visão Brokspace (o \"B\" dobrado na barra de atividades)\nencontra código pelo significado ou pelo nome; clique em um resultado para\nabri-lo.","**Busca que entende código.** Funções, classes e seções são indexadas\ninteiras e encontradas pelo significado ou pelo nome, em todos os\nrepositórios.","**Ask.** Type a question on the home page or in the agent panel: the\nBrokspace agent answers from your LLM with the sources it used; click a\nsource to open the file at that line. Follow-up questions keep the\nconversation. Press `Ctrl+Shift+A` (`Cmd+Shift+A` on macOS) for **agent\nfocus mode**, where the agent takes most of the window.","**Arrow IPC**: each commit writes a new immutable generation file and flips\n`CURRENT`. Files are memory-mapped and decoded zero-copy; immutability is\nwhat makes `mmap` sound and lets readers keep an old generation (Windows\ncannot replace a mapped file). Vector search is exact (dot product over\nnormalized vectors).","**Apple Silicon**: memory is unified, so a 16 GB Mac runs 7B/8B models fast.","**API keys** are never written to files: export them in your shell\n(`export ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=...`, or `$env:ANTHROPIC_API_KEY = \"...\"` in\nPowerShell) and Brokspace reads them when needed. Secrets found in your code\nare removed from the context before anything is sent to an LLM.","**Answers with sources.** Ask your own LLM (Ollama, LM Studio, or a hosted\nmodel) about the workspace; every answer lists the code it used.","**Aider**: `aider --model ollama/qwen2.5-coder:7b` inside your git\nrepository (`pip install aider-chat`, Python 3.10 to 3.12).","**Abra uma pasta** (Arquivo > Abrir Pasta). Se ela ainda não tem um\nworkspace Brokspace, a visão Brokspace oferece **Configurar Workspace**:\nela roda `brok init` para você.","**About AI reviews.** With a local 7b model, `brok review` is a quick first\npass: it catches slips you would rather not push, but it also gets things\nwrong (we have seen it invent a missing validation). Read its findings as\nquestions, not verdicts. For a review you want to rely on, use a 14b model\nor a hosted one for that run: `brok review -p anthropic` (see\nConfigure for API keys).","**2. Skills.** Exports the skills to `.claude/skills/` (Claude\nCode) and `.agents/skills/` (Codex, Cursor, Copilot and others), so `/ask-brok`,\n`/grill-me`, `tdd`, `code-review` and the rest are available in the agent.","**1. MCP server.** Registers `brok mcp` (a stdio\nModel Context Protocol server) so the\nagent gets two tools:",{"_1838":5611,"_1839":5612,"_1840":5613,"_1841":5614,"_1842":5615,"_1843":5616,"_1844":5617,"_1845":5618,"_1846":5619,"_1847":5620,"_1848":5621,"_1849":5622,"_1850":5623,"_1851":5624,"_1852":5625,"_1853":5626,"_1854":5627,"_1855":5628,"_1856":5629,"_1857":5630,"_1858":5631,"_1859":5632,"_1860":5633,"_1861":5634,"_1862":5635,"_1863":5636,"_1864":5637,"_1865":5638,"_1866":5639,"_1867":5640,"_1868":5641,"_1869":5642,"_1870":5643,"_1871":5644,"_1872":5645,"_1873":5646,"_1874":5647,"_1875":5648,"_1876":5649,"_1877":5650,"_1878":5651,"_1879":5652,"_1880":5653,"_1881":5654,"_1882":5655,"_1883":5656,"_1884":5657,"_1885":5658,"_1886":5659,"_1887":5660,"_1888":5661,"_1889":5662,"_1890":5663,"_1891":5664,"_1892":5665,"_1893":5666,"_1894":5667,"_1895":5668,"_1896":5669,"_1897":5670,"_1898":5671,"_1899":5672,"_1900":5673,"_1901":5674,"_1902":5675,"_1903":5676,"_1904":5677,"_1905":5678,"_1906":5679,"_1907":5680,"_1908":5681,"_1909":5682,"_1910":5683,"_1911":5684,"_1912":5685,"_1913":5686,"_1914":5687,"_1915":5688,"_1916":5689,"_1917":5690,"_1918":5691,"_1919":5692,"_1920":5693,"_1921":5694,"_1922":5695,"_1923":5696,"_1924":5697,"_1925":5698,"_1926":5699,"_1927":5700,"_1928":5701,"_1929":5702,"_1930":5703,"_1931":5704,"_1932":5705,"_1933":5706,"_1934":5707,"_1935":5708,"_1936":5709,"_1937":5710,"_1938":5711,"_1939":5712,"_1940":5713,"_1941":5714,"_1942":5715,"_1943":5716,"_1944":5717,"_1945":5718,"_1946":